## Source-integrity problems (identified and corrected)

1. **Schiphol evidence record URL (C-22):** The URL `news.schiphol.com/silence-at-amsterdam-airport-schiphol/` in the original evidence record describes an annual two-minute WWII commemorative silence (May 4), not Schiphol's general silent-airport operating policy. The claim is accurate and has been re-sourced to schiphol.nl/en/assistance and secondary trade coverage. Footnote [^22] records the discrepancy.

2. **Unknown evidence IDs (C-07, C-08, C-09, C-11, C-33):** Five evidence ID references in the pre-gate lineage pointed to records that do not exist in the evidence ledger (`regulatory-political-analyst::ev-ada35160`, `airline-commercial-strategist::ev-slot_67`, `regulatory-political-analyst::ev-crs_in12504`, `airport-emergency-management-director::ev-crowdstrike`). These were removed from the lineage. The claims they supported were verified directly against publicly accessible primary sources (federal statutes and regulations, CRS IN12504, national press for CrowdStrike).

3. **DCA slot-exemption airline pairings (C-11):** The pre-gate draft swapped Delta and United destinations (Delta/SEA, United/SFO instead of Delta/SFO, United/SEA). The error propagated from research through humanization without being caught until this remediation pass. Primary source (CRS IN12504 via everycrsreport.com) confirms the correct pairings. The error is documented in footnote [^11].

4. **DOT rulemaking scope (C-09):** The pre-gate claim implied an active "real-time flight information" DOT rulemaking was confirmed. The confirmed December 2024 final rule covers wheelchair accommodations only; the broader rule was not confirmed. Footnote [^9] updated to reflect the actual confirmed rule.

