## Limitations and standing diligence items

The following items remain open as diligence actions for MWAA General Counsel and operations staff, as flagged in the draft footnotes. They are not fact-check failures — they are correctly characterized as open items in the draft itself.

1. **GC memo on U&L broadcast rights:** Whether the executed 2025 U&L grants signatory carriers broadcast rights inside the leased gate envelope is not on the public record (C-01, footnote [^1]).
2. **GC memo on MII carve-out:** Whether the executed 2025 U&L follows the industry practice of exempting safety-mandated capital from majority-in-interest provisions (C-32, footnote [^32]).
3. **Fire Marshal AHJ delegation:** The specific written delegation of NFPA 72 STIPA enforcement authority to the Airports Authority Fire Marshal's office is a GC confirmation item (C-05, footnote [^5]).
4. **MWAA Design Manual acoustic content:** Whether current tenant-standards volumes contain explicit acoustic performance criteria is not disclosed on the public index (C-02, footnote [^2]).
5. **NFPA 72 and ACRP 175 primary text:** Both are paywalled or inaccessible at document scale. The STI and SNR figures cited in C-03 and C-04 are cross-checked across 10–11 independent evidence records and are retained as qualified; the Authority's acoustic consultant should verify directly against the current edition of each standard.
